{
  "authorized_claim": "Conditional on the pinned published planar normal-variational nonintegrability result, the translation-reduced spatial positive-mass Newtonian three-body Hamiltonian is not completely integrable by meromorphic first integrals near the embedded nonzero-angular-momentum parabolic Lagrange phase curve. Consequently, the qualified WP2-MULTIQ-v1 atlas admits no complete shell-regular physically admissible meromorphic Liouville family on any domain containing that regular neighborhood.",
  "campaign": "WP4-LIFT-NI-v2",
  "claim_boundary": "A passing result is a conditional theorem extension and transfer proof. It independently checks exact KS quotient identities, two-spinor product reduction, chart compatibility inherited from frozen WP2 evidence, fixed-energy Sundman conservation and Poisson identities, shell-relative functional-rank descent, collision-free restriction, reflection splitting, fixed-nonzero-angular-momentum planar reduction, and the planar normal variational subquotient. It consumes, but does not rederive, the published 4x4 planar normal variational equation or its non-virtually-Abelian differential Galois or monodromy group. It excludes ambient-only rank that disappears on J=0 or K=0, gauge-dependent or chart-dependent upstairs functions, explicit clock-dependent functions, non-meromorphic and non-Liouville notions, nonzero-Xi magnetic dynamics, a general SO(3) quotient, triple-collision regularization, and an independent new derivation of the published planar obstruction.",
